{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Grouping by file type (components/, hooks/, utils/) scatters one feature across four folders — grouping by feature keeps everything a feature owns in one place, deletable as a unit.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Reserve shared folders for code genuinely used by more than one feature. A single-caller helper starts inside that feature's own folder, not in a shared dumping ground.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Enforce the slice boundary with a lint rule restricting cross-feature imports to a public entry point — without it, feature folders degrade back into the same coupling, just with different folder names.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
